Our findings are subject to three main limitations.
\textbf{(1)~Model and statistical scope.}
Primary experiments use Qwen3-32B; cross-model validation (LLaMA-8B/70B, Gemini Flash) covers count and BCS dimensions but not secondary analyses (TOST, SDGD, error taxonomy). TOST separability holds on the probability scale but is inconclusive on the logit scale. Single-seed greedy decoding limits point-estimate precision (residual SD${}\,=\,0.88$\,pp; Appendix~\ref{app:variance-decomposition}). All evidence is correlational; mechanistic confirmation remains future work.
%
\textbf{(2)~DocRED multicollinearity.}
DocRED's severe VIF (50.9) prevents reliable BCS quantification; semipartial $R^2{}\,=\,5.6\%$ is directional only (Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_factorial}).
%
\textbf{(3)~Experimental scope.}
Four English Wikipedia/Wikidata datasets in a zero-shot setting; few-shot, fine-tuned, domain-specific, and non-English scenarios remain untested. BCS predicts RE batch accuracy but not NER, where errors scatter across non-type modes (Appendix~\ref{app:relaxed-matching}). Cross-dataset consistency is converging evidence, not independent replication \citep{rothman-1990}.

